67	     * <p>
68	     * A subline may be any arbitrary number of disjoints segments, so the endpoints
69	     * are provided as a list of endpoint pairs. Each element of the list represents
70	     * one segment, and each segment contains a start point at index 0 and an end point
71	     * at index 1. If the sub-line is unbounded in the negative infinity direction,
72	     * the start point of the first segment will have infinite coordinates. If the
73	     * sub-line is unbounded in the positive infinity direction, the end point of the
74	     * last segment will have infinite coordinates. So a sub-line covering the whole
75	     * line will contain just one row and both elements of this row will have infinite
