186	     * <p>In order to identify open loops which start and end by
187	     * infinite edges, the open loops arrays start with a null point. In
188	     * this case, the first non null point and the last point of the
189	     * array do not represent real vertices, they are dummy points
190	     * intended only to get the direction of the first and last edge. An
191	     * open loop consisting of a single infinite line will therefore be
192	     * represented by a three elements array with one null point
193	     * followed by two dummy points. The open loops are always the first
194	     * ones in the loops array.</p>
195	     * <p>If the polygon has no boundary at all, a zero length loop
196	     * array will be returned.</p>
197	     * <p>All line segments in the various loops have the inside of the
198	     * region on their left side and the outside on their right side
199	     * when moving in the underlying line direction. This means that
200	     * closed loops surrounding finite areas obey the direct
201	     * trigonometric orientation.</p>
