[{'input': 'Build a PolyhedronsSet from a cube BRep given as 8 3D vertices and 12 triangle faces (index triplets). Then traverse the BSPTree to extract the faces and rebuild the BRep.', 'expected': 'The traversal returns the 12 triangular faces of the cube, with consistent boundary polygons, so the BRep can be reconstructed.', 'actual': 'Face extraction from the BSPTree fails or gives wrong results for the cube, e.g. missing or incorrect boundary facets, or an exception.'}, {'input': 'The same cube with one vertex position changed by a small amount (as in the attached BSPMesh2.java).', 'expected': 'The result should be the same as for the exact cube, with faces extracted correctly.', 'actual': 'The extraction works correctly, so the bug depends on the exact vertex coordinates.'}]

