es and power-of-two scales, a narrow slice of all possible cube BRep inputs. The valid domain is better covered than before. The exact cube (no perturbation) and one-vertex cases are legal inputs outside buggyIf, so they stay available as non-triggering examples.\n\nOverall the failures match the reported nature of the bug (vertex-dependent BSP boundary handling failure for a cube BRep), so the test is relevant."
